# ── Site media (site/public/intro, site/public/demo) ──────────────────────
#
# The large encodes are working-tree deploy assets, not repo content: /promote
# runs `vercel --prod` from the main checkout where they exist, and committing
# tens of megabytes of video to a public OSS repo to serve a landing page is
# not a trade worth making.
#
# But an untracked-only directory has a failure mode: a GIT-based deploy (or a
# fresh clone) serves a page whose <video> and poster URLs all 404. The hero's
# posters (its first frame and settled frame) are brand images, so they are NOT
# committed here: the pages load them by absolute URL from the brand kit
# (site/app/lib/kit-images.ts), which works on every deploy, and a Git deploy
# degrades to a poster-only hero instead of a broken one. The SMALL replay
# assets below are COMMITTED: the clip (about 290KB) and its poster.
#
# The directory globs must be `dir/*`, never `dir/`: git does not descend into an
# excluded DIRECTORY, so a negation inside one can never be reached.
site/public/intro/*
site/public/demo/*
!site/public/demo/runaway-agent.mp4
!site/public/demo/runaway-agent-poster.jpg
